#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md:53
msgid ""
"`Arc` stands for \"Atomic Reference Counted\", a thread safe version of `Rc` "
"that uses atomic operations."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md:55
msgid ""
"`Arc<T>` implements `Clone` whether or not `T` does. It implements `Send` "
"and `Sync` if and only if `T` implements them both."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md:57
msgid ""
"`Arc::clone()` has the cost of atomic operations that get executed, but "
"after that the use of the `T` is free."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md:59
msgid ""
"Beware of reference cycles, `Arc` does not use a garbage collector to detect "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/shared-state/arc.md:61
msgid "`std::sync::Weak` can help."
msgstr ""
